===Etymology 1===
{{zh-forms|t2=孃|note={{lang|zh|孃}}: “mother”}}

Not attested in pre-[[Tang]] texts. It may ultimately have been a fusion of {{ltc-l|女郎|lady|id=1,1}} ({{zh-ref|Coblin, 1994}}).

Alternatively, from {{och-l|女|id=1|woman}} with an attached suffix ''*-ŋ'' also found in {{och-l|卬|I for my part}} as against {{och-l|我|I}} ({{zh-ref|Sagart, 1999: 134}}). However, evidence for this suffix is sparse; Sagart only adduces these two pairs of words.

As yet another suggestion, it may be a loan from {{bor|zh|otk||anaŋ|your mother}}, from {{cog|trk-pro|[[*ana]] ~ [[*eńe]]||mother}} (whence {{cog-lite|tr|ana}} and {{cog|ug|ئانا}}) and {{m|trk-pro|*-iŋ||{{ng|second person singular possessive suffix}}}}, ({{zh-ref|Vovin and McCraw, 2011}}).

